/-!
# No fixed-point-free module for a non-abelian group of order `p * q`

This file proves `Work.Frobenius.Complement.no_fpf_module_of_nonabelian_pq`.

The mathematical content is the classical fact that a non-abelian group of order `p * q`
(`p ≠ q` primes) has no fixed-point-free module over a field in which `p` and `q` are invertible.
It is used in the Feit--Thompson development to rule out a Frobenius complement containing a
non-abelian subgroup of order `p * q`.

The key input is `Work.Frobenius.Complement.exists_fixed_of_isFpf_module`: if `T` of order `q` acts
fixed-point-freely on a nonzero finite-dimensional space `W` and `X` of order `p` satisfies
`X * T = T ^ s * X` with `s % q ≠ 1`, then `X` necessarily has a nonzero fixed vector.  Combined
with the hypothesis that `X` also acts fixed-point-freely this is contradictory.
-/

namespace Work.Frobenius.Complement

/-- **No fixed-point-free module for a non-abelian group of order `p q`.**

Let `T`, `X` be endomorphisms of a nonzero finite-dimensional `F`-vector space `W`, with `T ^ q = 1`
and `X ^ p = 1` for distinct primes `p`, `q` which are invertible in `F`.  If `T` and `X` both act
fixed-point-freely and `X * T = T ^ s * X` with `s % q ≠ 1` (i.e. the group generated by `T` and
`X` is non-abelian of order `p q`), then `W = 0` --- contradicting that `W` is nontrivial. -/
theorem no_fpf_module_of_nonabelian_pq {F W : Type*} [Field F] [AddCommGroup W] [Module F W]
    [FiniteDimensional F W] [Nontrivial W] {p q s : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hq : q.Prime) (hpq : p ≠ q)
    (hpF : (p : F) ≠ 0) (hqF : (q : F) ≠ 0) (hs : s % q ≠ 1)
    {T X : W →ₗ[F] W} (hTq : T ^ q = 1) (hT1 : ∀ w, T w = w → w = 0)
    (hXp : X ^ p = 1) (hX1 : ∀ w, X w = w → w = 0)
    (hrel : ∀ w, X (T w) = (T ^ s) (X w)) : False := by
  obtain ⟨w, hw, hXw⟩ :=
    exists_fixed_of_isFpf_module (F := F) (W := W) hp hq hpF hqF hs hTq hT1 hXp hrel
  exact hw (hX1 w hXw)

end Work.Frobenius.Complement
